
Three-Cheese Baked Macaroni and Cheese

This recipe uses a blend of sharp cheddar for flavor, mozzarella for excellent stretch, and Parmesan for a salty, golden crust.
• Prep time: 20 minutes
• Cook time: 25 minutes
• Servings: 6–8

Ingredients

• 1 pound elbow macaroni (or any ridged short pasta)
• 4 tablespoons unsalted butter
• 1/4 cup all-purpose flour
• 4 cups whole milk (warmed slightly)
• 3 cups sharp cheddar cheese, freshly shredded
• 1 cup mozzarella cheese, freshly shredded
• 1/2 cup Parmesan cheese, finely grated
• 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder
• 1 teaspoon Dijon mustard
• 1/2 teaspoon salt (plus more for boiling pasta)
• 1/4 teaspoon freshly ground black pepper
• 1/2 cup panko or traditional breadcrumbs (optional, for topping)

Instructions

1. Boil the Pasta: Preheat your oven to 375°F (190°C). Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil and cook the macaroni according to package instructions until just al dente (it will cook more in the oven). Drain and set aside.
2. Build the Roux: In a large saucepan or Dutch oven, melt the butter over medium heat. Whisk in the flour and cook for 1 to 2 minutes, stirring constantly to remove the raw flour taste.
3. Thicken the Sauce: Gradually pour in the milk while whisking vigorously to prevent lumps. Continue cooking, stirring constantly, until the sauce thickens enough to coat the back of a spoon (about 5 minutes).
4. Season and Add Cheese: Remove the saucepan from the heat. Stir in the Dijon mustard, garlic powder, salt, and black pepper. Add 2.5 cups of the cheddar, all of the mozzarella, and half of the Parmesan. Stir gently until the cheese completely melts into a smooth sauce.
5. Combine: Add the cooked macaroni into the cheese sauce and fold until every noodle is completely coated.
6. Bake: Pour the mixture into a greased 9x13-inch baking dish. Top evenly with the remaining cheddar, Parmesan, and breadcrumbs. Bake for 20 to 25 minutes until the edges are bubbly and the top layer turns a rich golden brown. Let rest for 5 minutes before serving.